module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.portable_value_map_order_is_process_random

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data portable_value_map_order_is_process_random: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "portable_value_map_order_is_process_random" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: the interpreter's portable value form -- the representation built to leave a frame, be content-keyed and cross a process boundary -- carries map entries in an order that differs between runs of the same program on the same input. v1.interpreter Value::Map holds an im::HashMap<CanonKey, Value>, whose default hasher is std RandomState (im 15.1 hash::map HashMap<K, V, S = RandomState>), so its iteration order is re-randomised per process; portable_value_from_ctx_at copies entries in that iteration order into PortableValue::Map, and portable_value_digest folds them in that order. A second, independent source of the same variance: value_hash hashes a Variant's type_name and variant_name through Symbol's Hash, which is the spelling's POINTER, so CanonKey hashes over variant-bearing keys are address-dependent even under a fixed hasher. HARM: two runs that computed equal values publish unequal portable forms and unequal digests, so any reader that compares, keys or stores portable values across runs sees a difference where there is none -- the type_env plan's content-addressed invariants (docs/plans/type-env-single-authority-design.md) and every cross-run differential over warmed values inherit it. In-process sharing is unaffected: equality there is structural (portable_value_eq) and the memo key is per process.",
    "RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder -- silent, found while deriving a producer-grain differential for gunbc#12890, where 95 of 264 warmed producers carried different portable digests between two arms whose claim verdicts were equal at identity grain (396/396). The mechanism above is READ from the code, not yet measured as the cause of those 95: the confirming controls are (a) one arm run twice must already disagree on digests of map-bearing producers, and (b) the leaf-line dump of a differing producer from both arms must be equal after sorting and unequal before -- both requested on srv1. Until they report, the attribution of the 95 to this row is a bet, stated as one.",
    "SCOPE, FROM TWO CENSUSES (2026-10-01, v1.interpreter at main). MAP ITERATION: of the Value::Map sites, the order-blind ones (len, is_empty, contains and lookup, fast equality, value_hash's commutative Map arm, byte accounting, portable size, sorted_map_keys, JSON serialisation through serde_json's BTreeMap) expose nothing. Two order-exposing surfaces reach .dag programs, and they are NOT this row: map_keys and map_values are classified HostUnspecifiedOrder in std.primitive_identity and refused by v2.lens.determinism determinism_compile_gate under the existing class host_ordered_collection_reaches_an_emitted_artifact; and to_string or string interpolation of a map renders entries in host order with no traversal-order fact, a gap in that class's territory routed to its owner (jolly-boar-500 via neat-boar-16, 2026-10-01). The Map's own iteration deliberately stays host-ordered: the emitted Rust realization is an im HashMap as well, so canonicalising only the interpreter would make the two realizations disagree. THIS ROW owns the two interpreter-internal surfaces that cross a process boundary: the portable form's entry order, and value_hash's consumers. VALUE_HASH: CanonKey's Hash and hash_fields_commutative are in-process; the one cross-run consumer is recorded_fixture content_hash_service_inputs, which keys recorded-fixture replay by value_hash of each parameter -- so a variant-bearing parameter got a process-random replay key, a cache-purity defect.",
    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed, and the repair is in the ENCODING, not at a consumer: portable_value_from_ctx_at sorts map entries by portable_value_cmp, a total order over content alone (symbols by spelling, floats by IEEE 754-2019 totalOrder (f64 total_cmp)), so every reader and the digest see one order; value_hash hashes a variant's type and variant names by SPELLING. CONTROLS, both red with the repair disabled and green with it when run by hand on the remote runner. They are #[cfg(test)] lib tests, which NO CI lane runs (gunbc.rung_drop rust_unit_tests_off_the_merge_path), so this repair is unenforced on the merge path until that drop is retired: portable_canonical_order_tests portable_map_digest_is_equal_across_two_processes (the test re-runs itself as two child processes and compares the digest of one 64-entry variant-valued map) and value_hash_of_a_variant_depends_on_spelling_not_address. KNOWN RESIDUAL, with its trigger: value_hash is a std DefaultHasher, whose output Rust does not promise to keep stable across toolchain versions, while the recorded-fixture keys it derives persist across runs; a toolchain bump can therefore re-key every recorded fixture silently. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: content_hash_service_inputs keys through the declared std.content_hash structural family (v1_rt atom_identity_hash and hash_combine, as portable_value_digest already does) rather than a host hasher, with a control that a committed fixture's key is a fixed literal grounded in that family."
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
